    #      commit's; the log directory records/logs/m5p2-p2, the phase's
    #      directory <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p2-p2. SPEC_PIN's default is
    #      5067dfcc..., the spec's blob at P2's doc commit (the P1 rulings
    #      added). The commit-message rule's fixtures name M5 part 2 P2.
    #  FS. The records are P2's two pairs, a .md and a .txt each: the pivot
    #      sample's records/m5p2-p2-<date>-<short sha> and the open check's
    #      records/m5p2-open-<date>-<short sha>, at P2's phase commit's short
    #      sha. The fixture control plants a sample pair and an open .md of this
    #      sha (counted, 3), a longer stem of this sha, an open .txt of another
    #      sha and P1's sample stem m5p2-p1 at this sha (none counted); the
    #      status admits this phase's log directory and those records, by what
    #      each alternative admits.
    #  FT. The sibling logs are FOUR: gate, test, negative and run. The phase
    #      changes no gate file, so no self-test log is due: the gate-file block
    #      is the earlier phases' (changes DM and DT), measuring from the diff
    #      that no gate file is in it and that no self-test log stands in the
    #      log directory, with its two controls. Every sibling prints a script,
    #      so SCRIPT_LOGS is the same list. Change FQ's branch names the
    #      self-test log, which no list holds now, so it never runs; its
    #      function and its two controls stand.
    #  FU. Planning's files are the TWO P2's doc commit holds, specs/0033 and
    #      ROADMAP.md, in the listing of modified files (specs/0032 is no
    #      longer one); a check that the doc commit touches exactly those two,
