    #      sha and P2's sample stem m5p2-p2 at this sha (none counted); the
    #      status admits this phase's log directory and those records, by what
    #      each alternative admits.
    #  FY. The sibling logs are FIVE: gate, test, negative, size and run. The
    #      phase still changes no gate file, so no self-test log is due (changes
    #      DM, DT and FT, measured from the diff). Every sibling prints a script,
    #      so SCRIPT_LOGS is the same list.
    #  FZ. The code commits' paths are widened as M5 part 1 P3's scan widened
    #      them (its change FG): .rs files under tools/size-probe/src/bin/ (the
    #      probe commit) and CHANGELOG.md (the phase commit) beside the earlier
    #      paths. Change FL's control, which refused M5 part 1 P3's probe commit
    #      against the narrower paths, becomes the same form ACCEPTING that
    #      commit against these; the refusals of M4 part 2 P1's phase commit
    #      (crates/emend/Cargo.toml and the licence copies), of the doc commit
    #      and of the null commit stand.
    #  GA. specs/0033 "Planning rulings on P1", ruling 12, as change FV: the
    #      script's one mktemp call is the working directory's, checked under
    #      TMPDIR by change FN; the generator asserts it is still the only one.
    #      "Planning rulings on P2", ruling 7, asks the gate alone for the
    #      counting library's line, so this script adds none.
    #  GB. NEW after planning's ruling on the independent check's A1
    #      (2026-10-13): a tests commit ("M5 part 2 P3: the external link tests
    #      that can fail", crates/emend/src/package/tests/extlink.rs alone)
    #      follows the CHANGELOG commit and is the phase commit, so FZ's
    #      "CHANGELOG.md (the phase commit)" now reads the CHANGELOG commit,
    #      the phase commit's parent. The range's commits are read from git, so
    #      no count changes (seven in the range: the doc commit and six code
    #      commits); the tests commit is a code commit by its prefix and its
    #      path, and the last code commit. Two checks are added: the phase
    #      commit is the tests commit by its subject, the CHANGELOG commit its
    #      parent (with a control refusing the CHANGELOG commit as the phase
    #      commit), and the tests commit touches that one file alone (with a
    #      control refusing the CHANGELOG commit).
    #
    # CARRIED TO M5 part 3 P1 from M5 part 2 P3's scan script (printed in
    # records/logs/m5p2-p3/scan.log; its changes FW to GB are above), generated
    # by <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p3-p1/gen/scan.py, every replacement
    # asserted to occur its stated number of times. What differs:
    #  GC. The phase is Milestone 5 part 3 P1's (specs/0034-charts-read.md, "P1:
    #      the feature, the anchors, the plots and series"): the doc commit
    #      pattern "M5 part 3 P1: commit planning docs (specs/0034, the part 2
    #      close-out rulings)" and the subjects "M5 part 3 P1: "; the base is
    #      part 2's close-out record commit, found as the doc commit's parent and
    #      checked by its subject ("M5 part 2 close-out record: "), with a
    #      control that refuses the base's own parent's subject, part 2's
    #      close-out doc commit's; the log directory records/logs/m5p3-p1, the
    #      phase's directory <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p3-p1. SPEC is
    #      specs/0034-charts-read.md and SPEC_PIN's default 730693f3..., its blob
    #      at the doc commit; planning's rulings during P1 stand uncommitted in
    #      the working tree, so a run gives PLANNING_SPEC (change AV). The
    #      commit-message rule's fixtures name M5 part 3 P1.
    #  GD. The records are P1's two pairs, a .md and a .txt each, as part 2 P2's
    #      form had them (its change FS): the charts sample's
    #      records/m5p3-p1-<date>-<short sha> and the open check's
    #      records/m5p3-open-<date>-<short sha>; no single records (change FX's
    #      size and API review stems are gone with their loop). The fixture
    #      control plants a sample pair and an open .md of this sha (counted,
    #      3), a longer stem of this sha, an open .txt of another sha and part 2
    #      P3's sample stem m5p2-p3-kinds at this sha (none counted); the status
    #      admits this phase's log directory and those records, by what each
    #      alternative admits.
    #  GE. The sibling logs are FOUR: gate, test, negative and run (part 2 P2's
    #      form, change FT). The phase changes no gate file, so no self-test log
    #      is due (changes DM, DT and FT, measured from the diff). Every sibling
    #      prints a script, so SCRIPT_LOGS is the same list.
    #  GF. The code commits' paths are part 2 P2's (the probe binaries and
    #      CHANGELOG.md of change FZ are gone) widened by the two manifests the
    #      feature charts touches, crates/emend/Cargo.toml (the crate commit)
    #      and tools/emend-copy/Cargo.toml (the tool commit). Change FZ's
    #      control on M5 part 1 P3's probe commit is a refusal again, as change
    #      FL had it; the refusal of M4 part 2 P1's phase commit stands, since
    #      its two licence copies are no code path, and the refusals of the doc
    #      commit and of the null commit stand.
    #  GG. The roles: two code commits, the crate commit and the tool commit,
    #      the phase commit. Change GB's checks of the tests commit and the
    #      CHANGELOG commit become the same form over the tool commit and the
    #      crate commit, each found by its subject: the phase commit is the tool
    #      commit, the crate commit its parent (with a control refusing the
    #      crate commit as the phase commit), and the tool commit touches its
    #      three files alone, tools/emend-copy/Cargo.toml, src/main.rs and
    #      tests/null_rewrite.rs (with a control refusing the crate commit).
    #  GH. Planning's files are the THREE the doc commit holds: specs/0034
    #      (added), specs/0033 and ROADMAP.md (modified), in the listing of
    #      modified files; the check that the doc commit touches exactly those
    #      three keeps change FU's form, its control refusing part 2 P3's doc
    #      commit (two files), found by its subject. The spec PLANNING_SPEC
    #      names is specs/0034.
    #  GI. specs/0033 "Planning rulings on P1", ruling 12, as changes FV and GA:
    #      the script's one mktemp call is the working directory's, checked
    #      under TMPDIR by change FN; the generator asserts it is still the
    #      only one.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M5 part 3 P2 from M5 part 3 P1's scan script (printed in
    # records/logs/m5p3-p1/scan.log; its changes GC to GI are above), generated
    # by <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p3-p2/gen/scan.py, every replacement
    # asserted to occur its stated number of times. What differs:
    #  GJ. The phase is Milestone 5 part 3 P2's (specs/0034-charts-read.md, "P2:
    #      axes, legend, pivot source, style; the catalogue"): the doc commit
    #      pattern "M5 part 3 P2: commit planning docs (the P1 verification and
    #      rulings)" and the subjects "M5 part 3 P2: "; the base is P1's record
    #      commit, found as the doc commit's parent and checked by its subject
    #      ("M5 part 3 P1 record: "), with a control that refuses the base's own
    #      parent's subject, P1's tool commit's; the log directory
    #      records/logs/m5p3-p2, the phase's directory
    #      <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p3-p2. SPEC stays
    #      specs/0034-charts-read.md and SPEC_PIN's default is 02485398..., its
    #      blob at P2's doc commit; planning's rulings during P2 (M to S)
    #      stand uncommitted in the working tree's specs/0034 (sha256
    #      0db9d7d8...), so a run gives PLANNING_SPEC (change AV) and the status
    #      admits the modified spec. The commit-message rule's fixtures name M5
    #      part 3 P2.
    #  GK. The records are P2's two pairs, a .md and a .txt each: the charts
    #      sample's records/m5p3-p2-<date>-<short sha> and the open check's
    #      records/m5p3-open-<date>-<short sha>. The fixture control plants a
    #      sample pair and an open .md of this sha (counted, 3), a longer stem of
    #      this sha, an open .txt of another sha and P1's sample stem m5p3-p1 at
    #      this sha (none counted); the status admits this phase's log directory
    #      and those records, by what each alternative admits. The four sibling
    #      logs (change GE), the code paths (change GF) and every placeholder
    #      a log prints declared by a root line of that log (change N; P1's
    #      attempt 1 was refused by it) stand.
    #  GL. The roles: P2's two code commits by their full subjects, the crate
    #      commit and the tool commit, the phase commit, as change GG's form; the
    #      tool commit touches its two files alone, tools/emend-copy/src/main.rs
    #      and tests/null_rewrite.rs (the manifest is untouched in P2), with the
    #      control refusing the crate commit.
    #  GM. Planning's files are the TWO the doc commit holds, specs/0034 and
    #      ROADMAP.md, both modified; the check that the doc commit touches
    #      exactly those two keeps change FU's form, its control refusing P1's
    #      doc commit (three files), found by its subject. The listing of
    #      modified planning files reads specs/0034 and ROADMAP.md.
    #  GN. NEW: the doc commit's message names each file the commit holds with
    #      its blob's sha256, one line "<path> sha256 <hash>" each (the form of
    #      every doc commit since P1's re-made 266c410), checked by the commit's
    #      own file list and blobs, with a control refusing the crate commit,
    #      whose message carries no such line.
    set -uo pipefail
    # specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7: this script's own standard error, kept and counted at the end.
    SELF_DIR0=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
    mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR0/out" || exit 2
    ERR=$SELF_DIR0/out/scan-${2:-none}.stderr
    exec 2>"$ERR"
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 2
    . scripts/counting.sh
    # Change FN (specs/0032 close-out ruling 1): every temporary file of this run
    # lies under <scratch>/tmp, <scratch> the phase's directory.
    TMPDIR=$(cd "$SELF_DIR0/.." && pwd)/tmp
    export TMPDIR
    mkdir -p "$TMPDIR" || exit 2
    
    unset EMEND_PRIVATE_DENYLIST
    DENY_FILE=$HOME/.config/emend/private-denylist.txt
    COAUTHOR='Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>'
    # The close-out's other line, which this range does not carry (change C): a
    # refusal control, never an accepted line.
    COAUTHOR_OTHER='Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>'
    # coauthor_ok <line>: the line is the one this range carries (change C).
    coauthor_ok() { [ "$1" = "$COAUTHOR" ]; }
    coauthor_refused() { if coauthor_ok "$1"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    T=$(mktemp -d)
    trap 'rm -rf "${T:?}"' EXIT INT TERM HUP
    EMDASH=$(printf '\342\200\224')
    HOST=$(hostname)
    FQDN=$(hostname -f 2>/dev/null || hostname)
    hits=0; err=0; bad=0; ctl_fail=0
    
    DOC_PATTERN='^M5 part 3 P2: commit planning docs [(]the P1 verification and rulings[)]'
    git log --format='%H' --grep="$DOC_PATTERN" >"$T/doc-matches"
    NDOC=$(count_lines "$T/doc-matches")
    DOC=$(git log --format='%H' --grep="$DOC_PATTERN" -n 1)
    [ -n "$DOC" ] || { echo "the phase's doc commit was not found" >&2; exit 2; }
    BASE=$(git rev-parse --verify "$DOC^") || { echo "cannot resolve the base" >&2; exit 2; }
    C=${1:?phase commit required}
    SHORT=$(git rev-parse --short=7 "$C")
    # Change AK: where the sibling logs and records are read from; the values as
    # given are kept for the input lines (change AO).
    if [ -n "${LOGDIR+set}" ]; then LOGDIR_IN=$LOGDIR; fi
    if [ -n "${RECDIR+set}" ]; then RECDIR_IN=$RECDIR; fi
    LOGDIR=${LOGDIR:-records/logs/m5p3-p2}
    RECDIR=${RECDIR:-records}
    # Four, two and two digits: a stem that begins another's cannot match the
    # other's records (change BY).
    DATE_GLOB='[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]'
    # The stems of the phase's record pairs, a .md and a .txt each (changes CH,
    # EY, FJ, FS, GD and GK): the charts sample's record and the open check's.
    # No single records (change GD).
    PAIR_STEMS="m5p3-p2 m5p3-open"
    NPAIR=$(printf '%s\n' $PAIR_STEMS | wc -l)
    # The phase's records (change CH), one list for every loop that reads them. A
    # glob that matches nothing is printed as written and fails the -f test of the
    # loop that reads it, so a missing record lowers the count.
    phase_records() {
      local s
      for s in $PAIR_STEMS; do
        printf '%s\n' "$RECDIR/$s"-$DATE_GLOB-"$SHORT".md
        printf '%s\n' "$RECDIR/$s"-$DATE_GLOB-"$SHORT".txt
      done
    }
    # Two files per pair stem (changes CO, EY and GD).
    NREC_WANT=$((2 * NPAIR))
    # The sibling logs (change BV), one list; every count below is derived from
    # it. Four, no self-test log (changes FT and GE): the phase changes no gate
    # file. Every sibling prints a script, so SCRIPT_LOGS, read by the shape
    # greps, the removal classification and the spec pin, is the same list.
    SIBLINGS="$LOGDIR/gate.log $LOGDIR/test.log $LOGDIR/negative.log $LOGDIR/run.log"
    NSIB=$(printf '%s\n' $SIBLINGS | wc -l)
    SCRIPT_LOGS="$LOGDIR/gate.log $LOGDIR/test.log $LOGDIR/negative.log $LOGDIR/run.log"
    NSCRIPT=$(printf '%s\n' $SCRIPT_LOGS | wc -l)
    STAGE=${2:?stage required: pre-check or final}
    case $STAGE in pre-check | final) ;; *) echo "the stage must be pre-check or final" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
    HEAD_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)
    # specs/0001 "Rules for every phase" (M1 part 3 P1 ruling 11): the phase
    # commit is GIVEN to the script and compared with HEAD, with a control that
    # refuses a fabricated commit, and the header prints both values and the
    # comparison. A header that reads HEAD and prints it twice asserts nothing.
    NULL_SHA=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
    full_sha() {
      # /usr/bin/grep explicitly: in this tool shell `grep` is a different
      # program (specs/0001, "Rules for every phase").
      printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C /usr/bin/grep -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'
    }
    is_head() { full_sha "$1" && [ "$1" = "$HEAD_SHA" ]; }
    not_head() { if is_head "$1"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    ID_EMAIL=$(git show "$C:scripts/privacy-identity.txt" | sed -n 2p)
    EMAIL_RE='[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9-]+([.][A-Za-z0-9-]+)*[.][A-Za-z]{2,}'
    
    P6=()
    while IFS= read -r line; do P6+=("$line"); done < scripts/privacy-patterns.txt
    printf '%s\n' "${P6[@]}" >"$T/p6-patterns"
    PRE_COMMIT=$(git log --format='%H' --grep='^T0 P6d: narrow the three path patterns' -n 1)
    [ -n "$PRE_COMMIT" ] || { echo "cannot find the P6d narrowing commit" >&2; exit 2; }
    git show "$PRE_COMMIT^:scripts/privacy-patterns.txt" >"$T/pre-all" ||
      { echo "cannot read the pre-P6d patterns" >&2; exit 2; }
    sed -n '8p'  "$T/pre-all" >"$T/pre1"
    sed -n '10p' "$T/pre-all" >"$T/pre2"
    sed -n '11p' "$T/pre-all" >"$T/pre3"
    cat "$T/pre1" "$T/pre2" "$T/pre3" >"$T/pre-patterns"
    printf '%s\n%s\n' "$HOST" "$FQDN" | sort -u >"$T/host-patterns"
    # f_home came in with part 2 P3 and is inherited here, not new in this run.
    # The two sentences that stood here claimed it was new and claimed that both
    # independent checks of THIS phase had found an absolute path in negative.log
    # and observed that no form could catch it. Neither was true of part 3 P1:
    # those were part 2 P3's findings, and the comment was carried over verbatim
    # from that phase's script, where it was true; part 3 P1's independent
    # check 3 found it committed there. A comment that asserts what a check found is a claim like
    # any other and goes stale when the script is reused, so this one now says
    # what the form DOES rather than who asked for it.
    #
    # What the form is for: the P6d patterns are narrowed to one host's
    # user-directory prefix, named here by description and not written out, and
    # the three pre-P6d forms are bare shapes, so a path under this machine's
    # home directory would otherwise match nothing. The description rather than
    # the shape is deliberate: the self-scan
    # above ran the pre-P6d forms over this source and caught an inherited copy of
    # this very comment that spelled the prefix, which is the same defect the part
    # 2 P3 scan.log was committed carrying. The form asks the property the T0 P6d ruling
    # states: no log or check answer names this machine's home directory. The
    # pattern is $HOME, read from the environment and never printed, so the
    # scan cannot leak what it is looking for.
    #
    # ONE EXEMPTION, and the reason it is not a hole. A first version of this
    # form counted every occurrence of $HOME and failed the scan on ROADMAP.md,
    # which names the private corpus directory. That is not a leak: CLAUDE.md
    # and ROADMAP.md both name that directory deliberately, committed by the
    # maintainer long before this phase, and the corpus rule quotes
    # it as the place the corpus lives. So the form exempts $HOME/$CORPUS_DIR
    # and nothing else. It counts OCCURRENCES, not lines, because the helpers
    # here use grep -c: subtracting line counts would let one line holding both
    # the corpus root and a real leak net out to zero. A control covers exactly
    # that line, and another proves the exemption is one directory deep, since
    # the repository itself sits beside the corpus under the same parent.
    CORPUS_DIR=emend-testing
    # The exemption is a whole path SEGMENT, not a prefix: a directory beside the
    # corpus whose name merely begins with the corpus name is a leak like any
    # other, and a control asserts that. The boundary is "not a filename
    # character" rather than "a slash or the end of the line", because the two
    # committed mentions are followed by a backtick and by a full stop, and a
    # boundary of slash-or-end would have failed the scan on ROADMAP.md while
    # still exempting the sibling directory. That needs the exemption as a regex,
    # the one pattern here built with -E, so the home directory must contain no
    # ERE metacharacter. Rather than escape it and hope, the run refuses to
    # proceed if it does: an unescaped metacharacter would silently widen the
    # exemption, which is the one direction this form must not fail in.
    case $HOME in
      *[][.^\$*+?\(\)\{\}\|\\]*)
        echo "the home directory holds a regex metacharacter; f_home would" >&2
        echo "  widen its exemption silently. Stopping rather than guessing." >&2
        exit 2 ;;
    esac
    
    f_nonascii() { count_bytes "$NONASCII_CLASS" "$1"; }
    f_ctrl()     { count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$1"; }
    f_emdash()   { count_matches -F "$EMDASH" "$1"; }
    f_session()  { count_matches -E '^Claude-Session:' "$1"; }
    f_p6()       { count_from_file -E "$T/p6-patterns" "$1"; }
    f_pre()      { count_from_file -E "$T/pre-patterns" "$1"; }
    f_pre1()     { count_from_file -E "$T/pre1" "$1"; }
    f_pre2()     { count_from_file -E "$T/pre2" "$1"; }
    f_pre3()     { count_from_file -E "$T/pre3" "$1"; }
    f_host()     { count_from_file -F "$T/host-patterns" "$1"; }
    f_home() {
      local out rc all corpus
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E -e "$HOME/[-A-Za-z0-9._]" -- "$1" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      all=$(printf '%s' "$out" | LC_ALL=C awk 'NF { n++ } END { print n + 0 }')
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E -e "$HOME/$CORPUS_DIR([^-A-Za-z0-9._]|\$)" -- "$1" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      corpus=$(printf '%s' "$out" | LC_ALL=C awk 'NF { n++ } END { print n + 0 }')
      printf '%s' "$((all - corpus))"
    }
    f_deny()     { count_from_file -iwF "$T/deny" "$1"; }
    # Change EQ: the substring form parts before used, kept for one control only.
    f_deny_substring() { count_from_file -F "$T/deny" "$1"; }
    f_email() {
      local out rc
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E -e "$EMAIL_RE" "$1" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ "$rc" -eq 1 ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | LC_ALL=C awk -v id="$ID_EMAIL" '
        { a = tolower($0) }
        a == tolower(id) || a == "noreply@anthropic.com" || a ~ /@example[.]invalid$/ { next }
        { n++ }
        END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    FORMS="f_nonascii f_ctrl f_emdash f_session f_p6 f_home f_host f_deny f_email"
    
    run() {
      local n
      n=$("$1" "$2")
      echo "  form=$1 count=$n"
      if [ "$n" = error ]; then err=1; elif [ "$n" != 0 ]; then hits=$((hits + n)); fi
    }
    check_ctl() {
      local label=$1 want=$2 n r
      shift 2
      n=$("$@")
      r=$([ "$n" = "$want" ] && echo as-expected || echo UNEXPECTED)
      echo "  control $label count=$n expected=$want: $r"
      [ "$r" = as-expected ] || ctl_fail=1
    }
    # bad COUNTS the failing structural checks (independent check 1 F7: it was a
    # 0/1 flag printed as a count); the verdict still reads it as "0 or not".
    structural() { echo "$1: $2"; [ "$2" = yes ] || bad=$((bad + 1)); }
    yn() { if "$@"; then echo yes; else echo no; fi; }
    rep() { printf "$1%.0s" $(seq 1 "$2"); }
    
    # The phase's directory, the one above this script's own (change AM).
    SROOT=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)
    echo "command: git rev-parse HEAD"
    # The invocation as run, the script's directory written as <repo> or <phase>:
    # an absolute machine path in a log is a defect (T0 P6d ruling).
    MAIN=$(pwd)
    inv_path=$0
    case "$inv_path" in
      "$MAIN"/*) inv_path="<repo>/${inv_path#"$MAIN"/}" ;;
      "$SROOT"/*) inv_path="<phase>/${inv_path#"$SROOT"/}" ;;
      /*) inv_path="<phase>/scripts/$(basename "$inv_path")" ;;
    esac
    echo "invocation: bash $inv_path $*"
    # Change AO: every environment input, on a labelled line, set or not, the
    # phase's directory and the home directory written as their placeholders.
    SPEC_PIN_SET=${SPEC_PIN+set}
    SPEC_PIN=${SPEC_PIN:-0248539876d833e772596aecdde0d1b8d609635c19a62b4f3e04e8ca527c1d05}
    scrub_input() { sed -e "s#$SROOT#<phase>#g" -e "s#$HOME#<home>#g"; }
    show_input() {
      if [ -n "${!1+set}" ]; then
        printf 'input: %s=%s\n' "${1%_IN}" "$(printf '%s' "${!1}" | scrub_input)"
      else
        printf 'input: %s is not set\n' "${1%_IN}"
      fi
    }
    for name in LOGDIR_IN RECDIR_IN RERUN_NOTE RERUN_FILES; do show_input "$name"; done
    if [ -n "$SPEC_PIN_SET" ]; then echo "input: SPEC_PIN=$SPEC_PIN"; else echo "input: SPEC_PIN is not set; the default, $SPEC_PIN, is used"; fi
    PLANNING_SPEC=${PLANNING_SPEC:-}
    if [ -n "$PLANNING_SPEC" ]; then echo "input: PLANNING_SPEC=$PLANNING_SPEC (change AV)"; else echo "input: PLANNING_SPEC is not set"; fi
    echo "input: TMPDIR=$(printf '%s' "$TMPDIR" | sed -e "s#^$SROOT#<scratch>#") (set by this script before its mktemp -d; change FN)"
    if [ -n "${PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE+set}" ]; then echo "input: PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=$PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE (as given; change FH)"; else echo "input: PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE is not set (as given; change FH)"; fi
    export PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
    bytecode_off() { [ "$(printenv PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE)" = 1 ]; }
    structural "PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE is exported as 1 for every command this script runs (specs/0032 P2 verification ruling 6; change FH)" "$(yn bytecode_off)"
    # Change AU: HOME and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, read by this script, labelled; the
    # values themselves are never printed.
    if [ -n "${HOME+set}" ]; then echo "input: HOME=<home> (read for the home-path scan and the phase's directory; its value is the placeholder's)"; else echo "input: HOME is not set"; fi
    if [ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY+set}" ]; then echo "input: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set (its value is never printed)"; else echo "input: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not set"; fi
    echo "about: M5 part 3 P2 phase diff $BASE..$C; HEAD at run: $HEAD_SHA"
    echo
    echo "## the three shape greps over this script's own source, before it is printed (change E)"
    echo "specs/0001: the shape greps run over a script before its log does. They"
    echo "run here, each with a control fixture that must score 1, and each must"
    echo "score 0 on this script's source."
    SHAPE='[$][(](yn|is|isnot|ynnot) .*(&&|[|][|])'
    BANG='[$][(](yn|is|isnot|ynnot) [!]'
    ASSIGN='[$][(](yn|is|isnot|ynnot) [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z_0-9]*='
    echo "  the first pattern, assembled at run time:  $SHAPE"
    echo "  the second pattern, assembled at run time: $BANG"
    echo "  the third pattern, assembled at run time:  $ASSIGN"
    f_shape() { count_matches -E "$SHAPE" "$1"; }
    f_bang() { count_matches -E "$BANG" "$1"; }
    f_assign() { count_matches -E "$ASSIGN" "$1"; }
    # Change FO: PYB, a Python call without -I -B, over this script's own source.
    # The word is assembled, so the source spells no call the form would count.
    PYW="pyth""on3"
    PYCALL="$PYW[[:space:]]+(-|[^[:space:]]+[.]py)"
    PYOK="$PYW -I -B( |\$)"
    echo "  the fourth pattern (change FO), assembled at run time: a call $PYCALL on a line not opening with a comment, not followed by -I -B"
    f_pyb() {
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -v -E '^[[:space:]]*#' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -E "$PYCALL" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -v -E "$PYOK" | count_lines /dev/stdin
    }
    printf 'x=%s(%s -c x)\n' '$' "$PYW" >"$T/g-pyb"
    printf '# %s -c x\n' "$PYW" >"$T/g-pyb-comment"
    printf 'x=%s(%s -I -B -c x)\n' '$' "$PYW" >"$T/g-pyb-ok"
    check_ctl "f_pyb on a fixture holding a call without -I -B (change FO)" 1 f_pyb "$T/g-pyb"
    check_ctl "f_pyb on the same call in a comment line (change FO)" 0 f_pyb "$T/g-pyb-comment"
    check_ctl "f_pyb on a call with -I -B (change FO)" 0 f_pyb "$T/g-pyb-ok"
    printf 'x %s(is [ a = a ] && [ b = b ])\n' '$' >"$T/g-shape"
    printf 'x %s(is %s f a b)\n' '$' '!' >"$T/g-bang"
    printf 'x %s(isnot %s%s /usr/bin/grep -q x f)\n' '$' 'LC_ALL' '=C' >"$T/g-assign"
    check_ctl "f_shape on a fixture holding the chained form" 1 f_shape "$T/g-shape"
    check_ctl "f_bang on a fixture holding the leading-bang form" 1 f_bang "$T/g-bang"
    check_ctl "f_assign on a fixture holding the assignment-prefix form" 1 f_assign "$T/g-assign"
    # Change BW: the same three forms after the negating helper ynnot.
    printf 'x %s(ynnot [ a = a ] || [ b = b ])\n' '$' >"$T/g-shape-ynnot"
    printf 'x %s(ynnot %s f a b)\n' '$' '!' >"$T/g-bang-ynnot"
    printf 'x %s(ynnot %s%s /usr/bin/grep -q x f)\n' '$' 'LC_ALL' '=C' >"$T/g-assign-ynnot"
    check_ctl "f_shape on a fixture holding the chained form after ynnot (change BW)" 1 f_shape "$T/g-shape-ynnot"
    check_ctl "f_bang on a fixture holding the leading-bang form after ynnot (change BW)" 1 f_bang "$T/g-bang-ynnot"
    check_ctl "f_assign on a fixture holding the assignment-prefix form after ynnot (change BW)" 1 f_assign "$T/g-assign-ynnot"
    g_shape=$(f_shape "$0"); g_bang=$(f_bang "$0"); g_assign=$(f_assign "$0"); g_pyb=$(f_pyb "$0")
    echo "  over this script's source: chained=$g_shape leading-bang=$g_bang assignment=$g_assign python-without-I-B=$g_pyb"
    self_shapes_clean() { [ "$g_shape" = 0 ] && [ "$g_bang" = 0 ] && [ "$g_assign" = 0 ] && [ "$g_pyb" = 0 ]; }
    structural "this script's own source holds none of the three shapes and no Python call without -I -B (change FO), checked before it is printed" \
      "$(yn self_shapes_clean)"
    echo
    echo "## the phase's commits by role"
    echo "  the phase commit given to this script: $C"
    echo "  git rev-parse HEAD at this run:        $HEAD_SHA"
    structural "the phase commit given to this script is HEAD" "$(yn is_head "$C")"
    structural "control: the same form refuses a commit that is not HEAD" \
      "$(yn not_head "$NULL_SHA")"
    structural "control: the same form refuses a short sha of the real commit" \
      "$(yn not_head "$(printf '%s' "$C" | cut -c1-7)")"
    echo "command: git log --format='%H' --grep='$DOC_PATTERN'"
    echo "  commits matching the pattern: $NDOC"
    echo "  the doc commit resolves to $DOC; its parent is the base, $BASE"
    echo "command: git log -1 --format='%s' $BASE"
    BASE_SUBJECT=$(git log -1 --format='%s' "$BASE")
    echo "    $BASE_SUBJECT"
    BASE_PREFIX='M5 part 3 P1 record: '
    base_is_closeout_record() { case "$1" in "$BASE_PREFIX"*) return 0 ;; *) return 1 ;; esac; }
    not_closeout_record() { if base_is_closeout_record "$1"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    echo "command: git log --reverse --format='%H %s' $BASE..$C"
    git log --reverse --format='%H %s' "$BASE..$C" >"$T/phase-commits"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$T/phase-commits"
    PHASE_PREFIX='M5 part 3 P2: '
    DOC_SUBJECT='M5 part 3 P2: commit planning docs '
    : >"$T/phase-docs"; : >"$T/phase-code"; nforeign=0; doc_after_code=0; last_code=
    while IFS=' ' read -r sha subj; do
      case "$subj" in
        "$DOC_SUBJECT"*)
          printf '%s\n' "$sha" >>"$T/phase-docs"
          if [ -s "$T/phase-code" ]; then doc_after_code=$((doc_after_code + 1)); fi ;;
        "$PHASE_PREFIX"*) printf '%s\n' "$sha" >>"$T/phase-code"; last_code=$sha ;;
        *) nforeign=$((nforeign + 1)) ;;
      esac
    done <"$T/phase-commits"
    NDOCS=$(count_lines "$T/phase-docs"); NCODE=$(count_lines "$T/phase-code")
    echo "  commits in the range: $(count_lines "$T/phase-commits"); doc commits: $NDOCS; code commits: $NCODE; without the phase prefix: $nforeign"
    echo "  the doc commits, as git lists them:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$T/phase-docs"
    echo "  the code commits, as git lists them:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$T/phase-code"
    FIRST_LISTED=$(sed -n 1p "$T/phase-docs")
    first_doc_is_pattern() { [ -n "$FIRST_LISTED" ] && [ "$FIRST_LISTED" = "$DOC" ]; }
    last_code_is() { full_sha "$1" && [ "$1" = "$last_code" ]; }
    not_last_code() { if last_code_is "$1"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    code_present() { [ "$NCODE" != error ] && [ "$NCODE" -ge 1 ]; }
    echo "phase: Milestone 5 part 3 P2 (specs/0034-charts-read.md) scan.log, stage $STAGE; run at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    # Change AN: the spec's hash this log pins, one hash, SPEC_PIN; the file as it
    # stands and as the phase commit holds it.
    SPEC=specs/0034-charts-read.md
    SPEC_SHA=$(sha256sum <"$SPEC" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    SPEC_AT_C=$(git show "$C:$SPEC" 2>/dev/null | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    echo "spec: $SPEC, sha256 $SPEC_SHA in the working tree and $SPEC_AT_C at the phase commit; the pin: $SPEC_PIN"
    echo "LOGDIR=$LOGDIR RECDIR=$RECDIR (as used)"
    SUP_DIR=$SROOT/superseded
    if [ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ]; then
      echo "rerun: $RERUN_NOTE"
      # Change AP: the directory the superseded files are kept in.
      echo "rerun: the superseded files named below are kept in <phase>/superseded"
      # specs/0001 "Rules for every phase": every sha256 a log cites, a superseded
      # attempt's included, is PRINTED BY A COMMAND run over a file that exists at
      # run time, never typed from memory. The note above names its predecessors;
      # these lines are what make those names evidence. An attempt that was not
      # kept is named as having no hash, and why.
      echo "command: sha256sum and wc -c over each superseded attempt named above"
      for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do
        if [ -f "$sf" ]; then
          printf '    %s  %s bytes  %s\n' "$(sha256sum "$sf" | cut -d' ' -f1)" \
            "$(wc -c <"$sf")" "$(basename "$sf")"
        else
          printf '    NO HASH EXISTS for %s: the file is not there at run time\n' \
            "$(basename "$sf")"
        fi
      done
      if [ -z "${RERUN_FILES:-}" ]; then
        echo "    RERUN_FILES was not set, so no attempt above is hashed by this run"
      fi
    fi
    # SERIALIZED as the coordinator arranged, with the measurement at entry
    # (change I, P2 verification ruling 6).
    n_cargo=$(pgrep -x cargo | wc -l)
    n_rustc=$(pgrep -x rustc | wc -l)
    echo "SERIALIZED: no other log run was in flight (the coordinator's arrangement); cargo processes at entry: $n_cargo; rustc processes at entry: $n_rustc"
    structural "no cargo or rustc process was running at entry" "$(yn [ "$((n_cargo + n_rustc))" = 0 ])"
    # One line per root (change I, P2 verification ruling 5).
    echo "root: <scratch> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p3-p2, the phase's directory, the name specs/0032 close-out ruling 1 gives it (change FN); <scratch>/tmp is TMPDIR, made if missing, and this run's mktemp -d working directory (the fixtures, copies and message files) lies under it, deleted on exit"
    echo "root: <phase> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p3-p2, the phase's directory on disk, the directory above this script's own (change AM); <phase>/superseded keeps superseded attempts"
    echo "root: <phase>/scripts stands for this script's own directory, which holds the script the invocation names and, in <phase>/scripts/out, its own standard error (changes R and Q)"
    echo "root: <home> stands for the home directory of the account that ran this script"
    echo "root: <repo> stands for the repository's top level, the directory this script cds to; scripts/counting.sh is sourced from it and every file scanned is read from it or from git"
    script_dir_is_scripts() { [ "$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)" = "$SROOT/scripts" ]; }
    structural "the script's own directory is <phase>/scripts" "$(yn script_dir_is_scripts)"
    phase_dir_is_m5p3p2() { [ "$SROOT" = "$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m5p3-p2" ]; }
    structural "the phase's directory is <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p3-p2 (change AM)" "$(yn phase_dir_is_m5p3p2)"
    # Change FN: TMPDIR and the working directory, with a control.
    tmpdir_is_scratch() { [ "$TMPDIR" = "$SROOT/tmp" ]; }
    under_tmpdir() { case "$1" in "$TMPDIR"/*) return 0 ;; *) return 1 ;; esac; }
    not_under_tmpdir() { if under_tmpdir "$1"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    structural "TMPDIR is <scratch>/tmp, the phase's directory's tmp (change FN)" "$(yn tmpdir_is_scratch)"
    structural "this run's mktemp -d working directory lies under TMPDIR (change FN)" "$(yn under_tmpdir "$T")"
    structural "control: the same check refuses a directory beside TMPDIR, not under it (change FN)" "$(yn not_under_tmpdir "$SROOT/tmpx/w")"
    if [ -n "$PLANNING_SPEC" ]; then
      structural "the spec in the working tree hashes to PLANNING_SPEC, planning's uncommitted copy (change AV)" "$(yn [ "$SPEC_SHA" = "$PLANNING_SPEC" ])"
      planning_spec_ctl() { if [ "$SPEC_AT_C" = "$PLANNING_SPEC" ]; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
      structural "control: the same comparison refuses the phase commit's copy against PLANNING_SPEC (change AV)" "$(yn planning_spec_ctl)"
    else
      structural "the spec in the working tree hashes to the pin (change AN)" "$(yn [ "$SPEC_SHA" = "$SPEC_PIN" ])"
    fi
    structural "the spec at the phase commit hashes to the pin (change AN)" "$(yn [ "$SPEC_AT_C" = "$SPEC_PIN" ])"
    # Change AP: every superseded file a rerun names lies in <phase>/superseded.
    rerun_files_kept() {
      local sf
      for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do
        case "$sf" in "$SUP_DIR"/*) ;; *) return 1 ;; esac
      done
      return 0
    }
    structural "every file RERUN_FILES names lies in <phase>/superseded (change AP)" "$(yn rerun_files_kept)"
    kept_ctl() { local RERUN_FILES="$SROOT/elsewhere/x.log"; if rerun_files_kept; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    structural "control: the same check refuses a file outside it" "$(yn kept_ctl)"
    key_unset() { [ -z "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY+set}" ]; }
    structural "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not set in this shell (change AU)" "$(yn key_unset)"
    key_set_ctl() { local ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=planted; if key_unset; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    structural "control: the same check refuses a shell where it is set" "$(yn key_set_ctl)"
    dirs_default() { [ "$LOGDIR" = records/logs/m5p3-p2 ] && [ "$RECDIR" = records ]; }
    structural "LOGDIR and RECDIR are the defaults, so this is not a dry run (change AK)" "$(yn dirs_default)"
    apart() { case "$1/" in "$2"/*) return 1 ;; esac; case "$2/" in "$1"/*) return 1 ;; esac; return 0; }
    together() { if apart "$1" "$2"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    structural "this run's working directory and <repo> are distinct directories, neither inside the other (change FP)" "$(yn apart "$T" "$MAIN")"
    structural "control: the same form refuses a root inside the other" "$(yn together "$SROOT/scripts" "$SROOT")"
    structural "the doc commit pattern matches exactly one commit" "$(yn [ "$NDOC" = 1 ])"
    structural "the base is M5 part 3 P1's record commit, by its subject (change GJ)" "$(yn base_is_closeout_record "$BASE_SUBJECT")"
    structural "control: the same form refuses P1's tool commit's subject, the base's parent's (change GJ)" \
      "$(yn not_closeout_record "M5 part 3 P1: emend-copy --charts-sample")"
    echo
    echo "## the records this phase writes, by stem (changes CA, EY and FJ)"
    echo "  the pair stems, a .md and a .txt each, -<date>-$SHORT: $PAIR_STEMS ($NPAIR)"
    echo "  record files expected: $NREC_WANT"
    # count_found <dir>: the phase's records found in <dir>, by the same list the
    # scan below reads; the control runs it over a fixture directory (change CA).
    count_found() {
      local RECDIR=$1 n=0 f
      for f in $(phase_records); do [ -f "$f" ] && n=$((n + 1)); done
      printf '%s' "$n"
    }
    mkdir -p "$T/c-rec"
    : >"$T/c-rec/m5p3-p2-2026-01-01-$SHORT.md"
    : >"$T/c-rec/m5p3-p2-2026-01-01-$SHORT.txt"
    : >"$T/c-rec/m5p3-open-2026-01-01-$SHORT.md"
    : >"$T/c-rec/m5p3-p2-x-2026-01-01-$SHORT.md"
    : >"$T/c-rec/m5p3-open-2026-01-01-0000000.txt"
    : >"$T/c-rec/m5p3-p1-2026-01-01-$SHORT.md"
    check_ctl "count_found on a fixture with one sample pair and one open record of this sha, a longer stem of this sha, an open record of another sha and P1's sample stem at this sha, same command form (changes DE, EY, FS, GD and GK)" 3 count_found "$T/c-rec"
    structural "every commit of the range carries the phase's subject prefix" "$(yn [ "$nforeign" = 0 ])"
    docs_present() { [ "$NDOCS" != error ] && [ "$NDOCS" -ge 1 ]; }
    structural "the range holds at least one doc commit" "$(yn docs_present)"
    structural "the first doc commit listed is the one the pattern found" "$(yn first_doc_is_pattern)"
    structural "the range holds at least one code commit (changes EO and EZ)" "$(yn code_present)"
    structural "no doc commit follows a code commit" "$(yn [ "$doc_after_code" = 0 ])"
    # Change DK: each commit's role by the paths it touches. role_paths_ok
    # <commit> <ERE>: the commit touches at least one path and every path it
    # touches matches the pattern. It prints nothing.
    DOC_PATHS='^(specs/[^/]+[.]md|ROADMAP[.]md)$'
    CODE_PATHS='^(crates/emend/Cargo[.]toml|crates/emend/src/.+[.]rs|tools/emend-copy/Cargo[.]toml|tools/emend-copy/(src|tests)/[^/]+[.]rs|scripts/[^/]+[.]sh)$'
    role_paths_ok() {
      local n m
      git diff-tree --no-commit-id --name-only -r "$1" >"$T/role-paths" 2>/dev/null || return 1
      n=$(count_lines "$T/role-paths")
      m=$(count_matches -E "$2" "$T/role-paths")
      [ "$n" != error ] || return 1
      [ "$m" != error ] || return 1
      [ "$n" -gt 0 ] || return 1
      [ "$n" = "$m" ]
    }
    role_paths_refused() { if role_paths_ok "$1" "$2"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
