specs/0024 "Planning rulings during P2" ruling 1 (committed at M3 part 2 P3's doc commit; change CI):
a script removes recursively only a directory it created in that run, and a
script written or changed from P2 on writes the target as a quoted
${NAME:?} expansion, alone or with a path after it inside the quotes; the
committed scripts' existing forms stand. Each removal written as a command
is classified ruled, standing (a committed scripts/ line, outside a printed
script block) or unruled; unruled must be 0. Lines are named by number,
never printed.
